workedExamples.solution_text:
Calculate the angles between consecutive radials.
$\begin{aligned}\angle AOB&=140^{\circ}-40^{\circ}=100^{\circ}\\\angle BOC&=260^{\circ}-140^{\circ}=120^{\circ}\\\angle COA&=(360^{\circ}-260^{\circ})+40^{\circ}=140^{\circ}\end{aligned}$
The triangles surround $O$ completely: $100^{\circ}+120^{\circ}+140^{\circ}=360^{\circ}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (50:2.4);
\coordinate (B) at (-50:2.7);
\coordinate (C) at (-170:2.1);
\draw (O)--(A) (O)--(B) (O)--(C);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\path (O)--(A) node[pos=0.7,above left] {$80$};
\path (O)--(B) node[pos=0.7,above right] {$90$};
\path (O)--(C) node[pos=0.7,above] {$70$};
\draw (-50:0.45) arc[start angle=-50,end angle=50,radius=0.45];
\draw (-170:0.55) arc[start angle=-170,end angle=-50,radius=0.55];
\draw (50:0.65) arc[start angle=50,end angle=190,radius=0.65];
\path (0:0.9) node {$100^{\circ}$};
\path (-110:0.95) node {$120^{\circ}$};
\path (120:1) node {$140^{\circ}$};
\path (A) node[above] {$A$};
\path (B) node[below right] {$B$};
\path (C) node[left] {$C$};
\path (O) node[below left] {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find each triangle's area, keeping unrounded values for the total.
$\begin{aligned}A_{AOB}&=\tfrac12(80)(90)\sin100^{\circ}=3545.307910\ldots\text{ m}^{2}\\A_{BOC}&=\tfrac12(90)(70)\sin120^{\circ}=2727.980021\ldots\text{ m}^{2}\\A_{COA}&=\tfrac12(70)(80)\sin140^{\circ}=1799.805307\ldots\text{ m}^{2}\end{aligned}$
$\begin{aligned}A_{\text{total}}&=A_{AOB}+A_{BOC}+A_{COA}\\&=8073.093239\ldots\text{ m}^{2}\\A_{\text{total in ha}}&=8073.093239\ldots\div10\,000\\&\approx0.81\text{ ha}\end{aligned}$

