Use the cosine rule for each external side.
$\begin{aligned}DE&=\sqrt{40^{2}+50^{2}-2(40)(50)\cos100^{\circ}}\\&=69.242997\ldots\text{ m}\\EF&=\sqrt{50^{2}+30^{2}-2(50)(30)\cos120^{\circ}}\\&=70\text{ m}\\FD&=\sqrt{30^{2}+40^{2}-2(30)(40)\cos140^{\circ}}\\&=65.867341\ldots\text{ m}\end{aligned}$
The radials are internal survey lines, so exclude them from the fencing length.
$\begin{aligned}P&=DE+EF+FD\\&=69.242997\ldots+70+65.867341\ldots\\&\approx205.1\text{ m}\end{aligned}$

workedExamples.question_text:
A radial survey gives $OB=30\text{ m}$, $OC=25\text{ m}$ and a true bearing of $120^{\circ}$ for $B$ from $O$. Triangle $BOC$ has area $300\text{ m}^{2}$ and its angle at $O$ is acute. The diagram shows $C$ clockwise from $B$. Find the bearing of $C$ from $O$, to the nearest degree.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (-30:2.4);
\coordinate (C) at (-83.130102:2);
\draw[->,dashed] (O)--(0,1.6);
\path (0,1.6) node[above] {$N$};
\draw (O)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\path (O)--(B) node[midway,above right] {$30\text{ m}$};
\path (O)--(C) node[midway,left] {$25\text{ m}$};
\path (B) node[right] {$B\;(120^{\circ})$};
\path (C) node[below] {$C$};
\path (O) node[left] {$O$};
\path (1.2,-1.1) node {$300\text{ m}^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
Rearrange the triangle area rule, then take the acute inverse-sine solution.
$\begin{aligned}A&=\tfrac12ab\sin C\\300&=\tfrac12(30)(25)\sin\angle BOC\\\sin\angle BOC&=\frac{300}{375}=0.8\\\angle BOC&=\sin^{-1}(0.8)\\&=53.130102\ldots^{\circ}\end{aligned}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (-30:2.4);
\coordinate (C) at (-83.130102:2);
\draw[->,dashed] (O)--(0,1.6);
\path (0,1.6) node[above] {$N$};
\draw (O)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\path (O)--(B) node[pos=0.65,above right,xshift=4mm,yshift=3mm] {$30\text{ m}$};
\path (O)--(C) node[pos=0.75,left] {$25\text{ m}$};
\draw (-83.130102:0.55) arc[start angle=-83.130102,end angle=-30,radius=0.55];
\path (1.1,-2.9) node {$53.1301\ldots^{\circ}$};
\path (B) node[right] {$B\;(120^{\circ})$};
\path (C) node[below] {$C$};
\path (O) node[left] {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Since $C$ lies clockwise from $B$, add the angle to the bearing of $B$.
$\begin{aligned}\text{Bearing of }C&=120^{\circ}+53.130102\ldots^{\circ}\\&\approx173^{\circ}\text{T}\end{aligned}$

